## 🏢 Frontend Architecture (HTML & CSS) — updated for 9:16

Dual-layer crossfader: a Base Layer for looping states (idle/thinking) and an Action Layer for one-off/audio-driven states (welcome, speaking, thank_you), blended with CSS opacity so switching is instant and gapless — no `src`-swap flash.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>AI Receptionist Video Handler</title>
  <style>
    /* Container maintaining the 9:16 portrait aspect ratio */
    .avatar-container {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 450px; /* portrait: constrain width, not height */
      aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
      background-color: #f0f0f0;
      border-radius: 12px;
      overflow: hidden;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .avatar-video {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover; /* fills the 9:16 frame; crops evenly if a source clip is landscape */
      transition: opacity 0.2s ease-in-out;
    }

    #base-player { z-index: 1; opacity: 1; }
    #action-player { z-index: 2; opacity: 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="avatar-container">
    <video id="base-player" class="avatar-video" autoplay loop muted playsinline></video>
    <video id="action-player" class="avatar-video" muted playsinline></video>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

> If a clip ever comes back landscape (e.g. an engine ignored the 9:16 setting), don't just rely on `object-fit: cover` — that crops the sides off instead of rotating. Re-export it portrait with ffmpeg before serving it:
> ```bash
> ffmpeg -i landscape_input.mp4 -vf "transpose=1" -c:a copy rotated_portrait.mp4
> ```
> `transpose=1` rotates 90° clockwise; use `transpose=2` for counter-clockwise depending on which way the source is rotated. Only do this if the source is genuinely sideways — don't rotate a correctly-composed landscape clip, re-generate it at 9:16 instead, since rotation crops content top/bottom compared to a clip actually composed portrait.

